<title>RUSSIA: Russian current account surplus widens in Q4 1996.</title>
<headline>Russian current account surplus widens in Q4 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's surplus on the current account balance of payments widened to $3.77 billion in the fourth quarter of last year from $760 million a year earlier, the Central Bank said in its bulletin.</p>
<p>It issued the following current account data data (figures in millions of dollars).</p>
<p>    WITH ALL COUNTRIES		Q4 1996   Q3 1996   Q4 1995</p>
<p>    Current account balance	  +3,772    +1,431	+760</p>
<p>     Merchandise trade		 +7,697    +4,507    +4,301</p>
<p>	  Exports (FOB)		 +24,822   +21,569   +22,382</p>
<p>	  Imports (FOB)		 -17,126   -17,062   -18,080</p>
<p>     Non-factor services net	 -2,122    -1,266    -2,355</p>
<p>     Income net			  -1,963    -1,862    -1,300</p>
<p>	 Investment income net	 -1,885    -1,765    -1,227</p>
<p>	  Interest payments (due)    -2,057    -1,908     n/a</p>
<p>CURRENT ACCOUNT EXCLUDING TRADE WITH CIS AND BALTIC STATES</p>
<p>					    Q4 1996   Q3 1996   Q4 1995</p>
<p>    Current account balance	  +4,082    +2,271    +1,070</p>
<p>     Merchandise trade		 +7,890    +5,500    +4,547</p>
<p>	  Exports (FOB)		 +20,284   +17,358   +17,385</p>
<p>	  Imports (FOB)		 -12,395   -11,858   -12,837</p>
<p>     Non-factor services net	 -1,956    -1,388    -2,135</p>
<p>NOTES - All Q3 data revised. Differences due to rounding. CIS is Commonwealth of Independent States.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
